WEBVTT

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.300
This girl is Kouyama Mitsuki.

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:03.900
She's twelve and dreams of becoming a singer.

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:06.830
But unfortunately, she only has one year left to live.

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:08.480
Her manager has been selected

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:11.490
and we went to Dr. Wakaouji's 
place to meet her, but...

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:14.840
...we have to keep her secret
from being exposed. It's terrible!

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.190
But hey, it's my job

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:19.580
to get her through all these problems.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:21.090
Well then...

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:22.900
I wonder what's going to happen today.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:23.500
Huh?

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:28.820
Do you understand?

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:29.760
Yes.

00:02:06.470 --> 00:02:08.930
Stop that at once, it's unladylike.

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:10.210
How can you...

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:13.350
...be so rude as to only worry about your skirt?

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:15.720
You should be more attentive while eating.

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:19.020
What is that sound?

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:21.540
I-It's nothing!

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:23.960
I'm sorry. I'll be more careful.

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:24.780
Good night.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:26.800
Ah. Wait a minute.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:28.590
I haven't finished talking to...

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:32.240
Honestly, I really have to keep her on a short leash.

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:37.400
That was close.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.610
H-Hello?

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:42.550
Ah. Mitsuki-chan? This is Ooshige.

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:44.160
Ooshige-san!

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:45.190
It's short notice, but

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:47.270
your debut single has been 
selected to go on the market.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:49.900
Eh?!

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:50.970
Debut?!

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:01.590
Mitsuki-chan.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:04.940
This is your producer, Takasu-sensei.

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:06.280
I'm Kouyama Mitsuki.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:07.400
It's a pleasure to be working with you.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:09.170
The debut concept is...

00:03:09.170 --> 00:03:11.130
...the trouble of coming up with a cool and elite name.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:13.200
Um... could you repeat that?

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:15.560
If it's regarding that matter...

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:17.800
...there is no question about my supporting you.

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:18.580
I'm looking forward to working with you.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:20.610
What?

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:22.280
There's no need for you to worry.

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:23.940
Together, we'll be sure to...

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:26.920
...turn you into a sexy singer.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:29.890
S-Sexy you said?

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:31.920
What... you're going to be late?

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:32.630
Okay.

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:36.440
Here...

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:39.850
This is a song written just for your debut.

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:44.530
Love... me... do...?

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:47.570
"Love me do Forever".

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:49.340
You're a high school student, aren't you?

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:50.410
Don't you recognize English?

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:51.730
Uh, yes!

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:53.040
Sorry about that!

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:56.390
A tempting kiss...

00:03:56.390 --> 00:04:00.360
The two of us are already 
a Non-Stop Love Hurricane?

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:02.280
For now...

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:04.790
...we're concentrating on your debut.

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:05.460
Um...

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:05.800
Huh?

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.300
You want me to sing this?

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:11.430
Are you unsatisfied with it?

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:14.010
To say unsatisfied... well...

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:15.340
This is...

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:17.270
P-Please excuse us for a second!

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:23.450
You mustn't, Mitsuki-chan.

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:25.190
You have to be more happy about it.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:26.540
Takasu-san is...

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:28.280
...the one who produced Matsushita Genki's and...

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:30.330
...Kobayashi's debut.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:32.890
He's an amazing record producer.

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:33.530
Okay...

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.070
But...

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:37.980
...that song won't... be able to reach Eichi-kun.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:38.830
Eichi-kun?

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:42.460
Why don't you try writing one yourself then?

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:46.730
You just said that you wanted to put
your own feelings into your song, right?

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:49.470
So then, you'll have to try writing it yourself.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:52.930
My feelings in my song...?

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:55.890
Why don't you try doing it... songwriting?

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:01.390
I'm leaving this to you, Mitsuki-chan.

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:04.870
Man... these new artist nowadays are all so spoiled.

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:05.610
Well...

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:07.480
...it's okay as long as you understand how futile it is.

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:09.320
I'll try songwriting.

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:10.360
Eh?!

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:12.370
It's just like you said.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:14.600
I'll try to put my feelings in it.

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:16.970
Thank you very much for the advice.

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:19.540
That wasn't supposed to be advice...

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:21.870
What? That's bad...

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:24.300
Got it. I'll be right there.

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:27.590
It's fine. This'll be interesting.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:30.510
However, the time limit is three days.

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:34.490
Just how far can you go in three days.

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:36.220
I want you to show me that.

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:40.180
I... I'm very sorry!

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:45.640
Mitsuki-chan.

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:46.270
Yes?

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:50.530
As your manager, there's something I want to ask you.

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:51.600
Y-Yes?

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:53.470
Who's Eichi-kun?

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:55.160
Tell me!

00:05:58.200 --> 00:05:59.370
I see...

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:01.610
So you have someone you like.

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:02.200
Yes.

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:06.870
But he left for America, and I
haven't had any contact with him.

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:09.040
My desire to become a singer is because...

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:10.710
...if he heard me...

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:12.590
...then maybe he'd notice me.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:13.990
That's what I think.

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:16.190
All right!

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:17.010
Huh?

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:19.800
If that's the case, then I'll be rooting for you.

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:21.010
Really?

00:06:21.010 --> 00:06:21.800
Yep.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:22.890
That song just now...

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:25.420
...had no musical sense or good points to it at all.

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:27.400
But... it'll be popular, right?

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:30.590
You don't need to restrict yourself
to only song that will be popular.

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:35.590
I want you... to debut with a good song.

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:37.660
Ooshige-san...

00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:39.350
Write a good song...

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:41.500
...and open Takasu-san's eyes!

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:42.120
Okay!

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:49.980
All right...

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:50.750
...let's start writing!

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:58.660
What's wrong? Hurry up and write.

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:00.460
I'd like to do that, but...

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:03.480
I wonder how I'm supposed 
to go about songwriting...

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:04.270
Don't tell me...

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:05.850
...you don't know how to write songs!

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:07.020
Yeah...

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:10.360
Then why did you say you were going to write a song?!

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:14.800
You have to be more upbeat when you're 
songwriting instead of suffering like you are now.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:15.870
What should I do?

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:17.320
I have to finish it in three days...

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:20.770
Just leave it to me.

00:07:21.490 --> 00:07:24.240
Do you have any CDs of a song anthology?

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:25.540
Yup. Just a sec.

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:31.410
Do you always keep it there?

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:34.080
Yup, it's easier for me to find them this way.

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:35.670
See.

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:40.140
That looks like it, but it's so worn out...

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:44.600
This is the only thing I have that's music-related.

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:47.730
I've read it over and over again.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:51.730
You're really so... valiant!

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:53.540
By the way, Meroko...

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:55.590
...what do you plan on doing about your song?

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:57.820
Well, that's...

00:07:58.860 --> 00:07:59.820
Eh?

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:03.440
Meroko, what the hell are doing all of a sudden?!

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:07.040
I can't understand what you're saying!

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.470
Anyways...

00:08:09.470 --> 00:08:10.970
...let go of my ha-...!

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:14.660
What I just did was a hint.

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:15.250
Eh?

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:17.630
So then, what was it?

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:19.160
What the hell do you mean, "What is it?"

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:20.970
All you did back there was clamp 
your big mouth over my hand!

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:22.280
Exactly.

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:23.720
You should just shut your mouth.

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:27.240
But... I wonder if I'll be okay doing something like that.

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:29.020
Of course not, there's no way you'll be okay!

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:30.600
It'll be fine.

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:33.800
You're doing this to see the
person you like, after all.

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:35.560
I guess so...

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:37.330
Huh?

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:38.960
Do whatever you want!

00:08:46.030 --> 00:08:48.080
W-What was that for?

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:53.540
Now Takuto will be all lovey-dovey with me.

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:55.250
Man...

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:57.720
You said to leave the songwriting to you...

00:08:57.720 --> 00:08:59.180
and you're already sick of it.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:08:59.510
Huh?

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:25.740
I guess it can't be helped.

00:09:42.950 --> 00:09:44.080
You're up early.

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:45.720
Ah, Takuto.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:47.140
Good morning.

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:53.190
By the way, are you okay in just your pajamas?

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:54.990
Yeah. I seem fine.

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:57.340
I guess I forgot about my sickness.

00:09:57.340 --> 00:09:58.650
Forgot...?

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:03.150
It's the first time I've ever
forgotten about my sickness.

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:06.210
Doing what I want to, with all my heart...

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:07.620
...it feels so good.

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:11.010
And... it was you, right?

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:11.620
Huh?

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:12.940
This.

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:16.290
That's why I'm fine.

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:18.010
Thank you!

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:22.540
A-Anyways, did you finish writing?

00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:25.110
Yeah. I finished writing, but...

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:27.720
What is it?

00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:28.970
Meroko.

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:30.600
Let's see.

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:34.360
H-How is it?

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:36.060
Well...

00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:38.500
How should I put it...

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:41.150
Huh? If you don't get it, then let me have a look at it.

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:44.990
<i>If you're smiling... it's like a clear day.</i>

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:47.200
<i>If you're crying... it's like a great flood.</i>

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:50.060
<i>As long as I am by your side,
it'll always be smiles and peace.</i>

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:51.620
What's this suppose to be?

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:53.620
As I thought... they're no good, huh.

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:55.700
I-I wouldn't say that they're no good...

00:10:55.700 --> 00:10:56.160
Y-Yeah.

00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:58.030
The first time's probably like this.

00:10:58.040 --> 00:10:58.920
It's okay.

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:01.290
I know that I can't do it by myself.

00:11:01.670 --> 00:11:04.210
I've never done it before, after all.

00:11:04.210 --> 00:11:06.150
There isn't time to learn.

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:08.760
Why don't you go on a date once, then?

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:09.720
Eh?!

00:11:09.720 --> 00:11:10.440
Sure.

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:12.110
If you do that, you'll be able to write something.

00:11:12.110 --> 00:11:13.810
But... how?

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:15.500
There's no one to go with.

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:16.190
T-That's right...

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:21.360
I thought it was a good idea...

00:11:24.570 --> 00:11:26.440
Good morning, Mitsuki-chan!

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:27.860
How are you feeling this morning?

00:11:29.610 --> 00:11:31.120
There he is!

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:32.920
The person who you're going on a date with!

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:33.640
Eh?!

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:35.370
A date with Wakaouji-sensei?!

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:51.970
Wow!

00:11:52.430 --> 00:11:55.930
This is the first time I've ever been to Harajuku!

00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:59.770
You're this happy about coming here... I'm glad.

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:03.860
I was really surprised when you
asked me on a date, though.

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:08.270
Well, as long as you're this
happy, your body will get better.

00:12:08.270 --> 00:12:08.840
Okay!

00:12:09.110 --> 00:12:09.880
All right!

00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:11.820
Let's start our date.

00:12:11.820 --> 00:12:12.530
Okay!

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:26.530
Wow!

00:12:26.530 --> 00:12:27.810
This is really good!

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:28.780
Isn't it?

00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:32.840
I was sure that you would like it.

00:12:32.840 --> 00:12:35.880
Just what you would expect from a little girl's escort.

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:37.730
Heh. He's not doing much.

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:40.000
So... how's the date?

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:42.020
This is more fun than your job, right?

00:12:42.020 --> 00:12:42.700
Yep!

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:44.770
I had lots of fun!

00:12:44.770 --> 00:12:48.170
It's almost as if I was on a date with Eichi-kun.

00:12:48.170 --> 00:12:48.900
Ah!

00:12:51.150 --> 00:12:53.290
Sometimes when you're staring at the sky...

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:55.640
...you're thinking about Eichi-kun, aren't you?

00:12:56.490 --> 00:12:58.670
Eichi-kun, Eichi-kun...

00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:01.460
She's so cute!

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:03.300
Well...

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:04.420
...it's about time.

00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:06.290
Shall we head back?

00:13:06.290 --> 00:13:07.060
Okay!

00:13:10.820 --> 00:13:11.840
Mitsuki-chan!

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:13.760
Are you all right?

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:14.870
Mitsuki-chan!

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:15.660
Yes.

00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:16.800
I'm fine.

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:20.370
Mitsuki-chan!

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:21.980
Mitsuki-chan, hold on!

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:24.520
Mitsuki-chan!

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:32.290
The medicine's taken effect, right?

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:33.740
Your fever's gone down,

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:34.990
and you don't seem like coughing anymore.

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:36.680
I'm sorry.

00:13:36.680 --> 00:13:38.500
It's because I was thinking selfishly.

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:39.210
No.

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:41.500
It was my fault for being careless.

00:13:41.830 --> 00:13:43.150
That's not it.

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:45.170
Last night... I stayed up.

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:46.640
You stayed up?

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:49.170
It couldn't have been because of your job.

00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:54.150
I certainly agreed to your working, but...

00:13:54.150 --> 00:13:56.220
...if you do such unreasonable things,

00:13:56.220 --> 00:13:59.650
I can't allow you to continue being a model.

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:03.100
Sensei! Please stop saying that!

00:14:03.510 --> 00:14:05.710
I want to debut no matter what!

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:06.770
If I don't debut...

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:10.200
...I won't be able to let Eichi-kun know that I'm here.

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:12.070
I... I...

00:14:14.270 --> 00:14:15.170
I understand.

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:18.040
You don't need to say any more.

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:20.290
If I oppose you, I'll just be the bad guy.

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:22.280
Don't worry.

00:14:22.280 --> 00:14:24.140
I'll still back you up.

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:25.290
Really?!

00:14:25.850 --> 00:14:26.710
Of course.

00:14:26.870 --> 00:14:29.360
But don't do anything unreasonable from now on.

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:30.230
Okay!

00:14:30.230 --> 00:14:31.900
Eichi again, huh?

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:35.560
To be thought about this much... Eichi must be happy.

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:38.340
I also won't do anything like... giving up on Takuto!

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:39.720
Let me go already!

00:14:40.970 --> 00:14:43.270
I'll excuse myself, then.

00:14:51.230 --> 00:14:52.560
What are you doing?

00:14:52.560 --> 00:14:55.080
The medicine's working, so I'll...

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:56.210
Stop it.

00:14:56.210 --> 00:14:57.440
Go to sleep.

00:14:57.440 --> 00:14:59.630
I can't fall asleep.

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:02.520
There's only one day left to write a song.

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:04.750
Hey, Takuto.

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:06.650
Can you turn me into a sixteen year old again?

00:15:06.650 --> 00:15:09.730
Then you won't have to worry about my health, right?

00:15:09.730 --> 00:15:11.480
That's true, but...

00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:14.100
Why do you have to do such unreasonable things?!

00:15:14.630 --> 00:15:15.760
Isn't it fine?!

00:15:16.340 --> 00:15:18.760
That producer Takasu's songs...

00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:20.950
...they'll be a hit, right?

00:15:20.950 --> 00:15:23.860
I don't want a song that's just a hit.

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:28.030
I have to send my feelings to Eichi-kun properly.

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:31.670
Just stop it already.

00:15:31.670 --> 00:15:32.270
Huh?

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:34.010
Takuto?

00:15:34.010 --> 00:15:36.350
Stop trying to write songs like that!

00:15:36.360 --> 00:15:38.190
What do you mean by that?

00:15:38.190 --> 00:15:39.640
Just give up already.

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:42.870
Besides, writing a song is impossible for you.

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:45.920
W-Wait... Hold up,

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:47.150
Takuto!

00:15:47.150 --> 00:15:48.300
Takuto!

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:49.290
Takuto!

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:06.220
What should I do?

00:16:22.110 --> 00:16:24.620
Takuto, wait up!

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:26.630
Wait up, I said!

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:29.230
What's wrong with you, saying something like that...

00:16:29.230 --> 00:16:29.820
Huh?

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:35.720
What's with you... stopping so suddenly...

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:36.480
Meroko.

00:16:36.480 --> 00:16:37.290
Huh?

00:16:40.880 --> 00:16:43.390
It kinda looks like they're arguing.

00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:44.940
Let's check it out.

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:46.640
Okay.

00:16:48.310 --> 00:16:49.720
What is the meaning of this?

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:53.350
What's "the song is already done" supposed to mean?

00:16:53.350 --> 00:16:55.430
Just what I said.

00:16:55.430 --> 00:16:57.820
The songs have been altered.

00:16:57.820 --> 00:16:59.030
That can't be.

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:02.040
Back there you promised Mitsuki-chan
she could write her own so-...!

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:06.400
...do you understand how much will be lost?

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:07.840
Leaving it to an amateur...

00:17:07.840 --> 00:17:10.670
...did you really think that I'd do that?

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:12.420
T-That's...

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:14.840
But, a promise is a promise!

00:17:15.380 --> 00:17:16.520
How naive.

00:17:16.520 --> 00:17:19.700
You can't think like that in this world.

00:17:21.330 --> 00:17:22.680
Ow! Ow!

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:24.010
Ow!

00:17:25.070 --> 00:17:26.320
Good job, you.

00:17:26.320 --> 00:17:27.460
Open your eyes.

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:29.980
There's no way someone like you could
ever understand Mitsuki's feelings.

00:17:42.490 --> 00:17:43.810
I'm going back.

00:17:44.100 --> 00:17:44.980
Wait!

00:17:44.980 --> 00:17:46.970
Geez... what's with you?

00:17:46.970 --> 00:17:48.590
Ow! That place hurts!

00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:49.450
Ow!

00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:58.040
Mitsuki...

00:17:58.600 --> 00:18:00.100
Back there, I...

00:18:00.560 --> 00:18:02.280
What are you doing?

00:18:02.280 --> 00:18:04.210
Hurry up and stop that.

00:18:08.210 --> 00:18:09.520
Back there, I...

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:10.270
Takuto...?

00:18:10.470 --> 00:18:11.180
Huh?

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:13.770
Then... this is...

00:18:14.120 --> 00:18:15.690
While I was writing my song...

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:18.590
...Grandma kept coming in and checking on me.

00:18:18.590 --> 00:18:20.230
So I pretended that I was under my blanket.

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:23.200
Wh-What in the..?!

00:18:23.420 --> 00:18:24.580
Takuto.

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:26.160
I'm sorry about earlier.

00:18:26.390 --> 00:18:28.920
E-Er... that's supposed to be my line.

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:33.160
I've been only depending on you guys for everything.

00:18:33.450 --> 00:18:36.450
Wanting to debut... and wanting to see Eichi-kun...

00:18:36.450 --> 00:18:38.420
...those are all part of my dream.

00:18:38.420 --> 00:18:40.130
If I don't work hard myself...

00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:41.580
...that'd be wrong, right?

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:47.130
You've been writing the whole time since then?

00:18:47.130 --> 00:18:48.030
Yeah.

00:18:48.030 --> 00:18:50.480
I've thrown away a lot of drafts.

00:18:51.140 --> 00:18:54.860
But it was fun to think this much about a song.

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:55.490
Eh?

00:18:56.100 --> 00:18:58.120
I really do love singing!

00:19:00.730 --> 00:19:03.670
Earlier, when I thought about 
never being able to sing again...

00:19:03.670 --> 00:19:05.280
...I was really sad.

00:19:05.280 --> 00:19:06.490
It was painful...

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:10.700
I want to see Eichi-kun, of course, but...

00:19:10.700 --> 00:19:13.550
...I want to sing just as much!

00:19:14.240 --> 00:19:16.960
This feeling makes my heart skip!

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:18.750
I can't make it stop!

00:19:20.330 --> 00:19:21.420
That's it.

00:19:21.420 --> 00:19:23.470
Eh? That's it?

00:19:23.920 --> 00:19:26.590
Use the true words that came from your heart...

00:19:26.590 --> 00:19:29.310
...try singing with those.

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:31.430
Put these feelings into my song?

00:19:31.760 --> 00:19:32.430
Yeah.

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:33.080
But...

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:34.600
I wonder if I can say it well.

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:36.890
You told me just fine.

00:19:38.520 --> 00:19:39.640
Me, too.

00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:42.180
Okay!

00:19:42.180 --> 00:19:43.820
I got it! I'll try it!

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:45.360
That's it.

00:19:45.360 --> 00:19:46.240
That's the spirit!

00:19:46.970 --> 00:19:48.600
Work hard!

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:49.390
Okay!

00:19:55.530 --> 00:19:58.140
This is the best I can do towards expressing my feelings.

00:19:58.140 --> 00:19:59.580
Please take a look at them.

00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:02.590
Well. I'll at least take a look at it.

00:20:11.800 --> 00:20:13.650
Well, it can't be helped.

00:20:16.350 --> 00:20:17.930
This is Takasu.

00:20:17.930 --> 00:20:21.590
For Kouyama Mitsuki's song, 
I've selected a different one.

00:20:21.590 --> 00:20:22.340
Huh?

00:20:22.340 --> 00:20:23.470
That means...

00:20:23.470 --> 00:20:24.640
I lost.

00:20:24.640 --> 00:20:26.720
Writing with such will...

00:20:26.720 --> 00:20:29.250
...the concept and the feeling... it's all there.

00:20:29.250 --> 00:20:30.410
That means...

00:20:30.670 --> 00:20:31.760
You did it!

00:20:31.760 --> 00:20:32.660
It's been accepted!

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:34.410
Your song's been chosen!

00:20:34.410 --> 00:20:36.580
Eh? Really?!

00:20:36.590 --> 00:20:39.000
Yes, even though you have a tight schedule.

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:40.370
It's all due to your rash actions.

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:42.440
Prepare yourself.

00:20:42.440 --> 00:20:43.590
It's going to be busy.

00:20:43.960 --> 00:20:46.020
Yes! We'll do our best!

00:20:46.020 --> 00:20:46.900
By the way...

00:20:46.900 --> 00:20:48.050
...what are you going to use for a stage name?

00:20:48.370 --> 00:20:49.030
Huh?

00:20:49.030 --> 00:20:50.210
That's right...

00:20:50.210 --> 00:20:51.020
What should we use?

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:52.350
Do you want to just go with your real name?

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:54.500
N-No, that'll be bad...

00:20:54.520 --> 00:20:56.100
Um...

00:20:58.140 --> 00:20:59.720
<i>Hey, Mitsuki.</i>

00:21:00.680 --> 00:21:03.740
<i>If by chance the two of us are separated...</i>

00:21:03.740 --> 00:21:05.540
<i>...there's no need to worry.</i>

00:21:05.540 --> 00:21:07.000
<i>Why?</i>

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:09.660
<i>Even if we're at the ends of the world...</i>

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:10.950
<i>...the moon will be in the sky.</i>

00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:15.720
<i>So, I'll look in the sky for the moon...</i>

00:21:15.720 --> 00:21:18.980
<i>That's why you have to shine even brighter...</i>

00:21:18.980 --> 00:21:21.190
<i>...so that I can find you sooner.</i>

00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:28.930
I've decided.

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:31.860
I've chosen Full Moon.

00:23:06.340 --> 00:23:08.270
Yo-re-i-ho!

00:23:09.260 --> 00:23:10.560
That's because... look, look...

00:23:10.580 --> 00:23:11.420
...at this setting.

00:23:11.420 --> 00:23:13.440
A blue sky. Green mountains.

00:23:13.440 --> 00:23:15.600
The air is so fresh...

00:23:16.780 --> 00:23:18.740
This is her first job, after all.

00:23:18.760 --> 00:23:20.460
We have to keep an eye on her.

00:23:21.490 --> 00:23:23.650
But I wonder if that girl can pull it off.

00:23:24.240 --> 00:23:25.370
When you say that...

00:23:25.370 --> 00:23:27.860
Inside, she's still a twelve year old...

00:23:28.080 --> 00:23:30.250
Next time on Full Moon wo Sagashite:

00:23:30.250 --> 00:23:31.580
The First Job.
